{"availability":"available","full":"GIFTEDLOV/firewall","name":"firewall","description":"Semantic execution security for on-chain governance.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-08T09:52:57Z","updated":"2026-10-08T23:37:58Z","branch":"master","homepage":"https://firewall-xi.vercel.app","topics":["genlayer","governance","nextjs","onchain-governance","security","semantic-security","smart-contracts","typescript","web3"],"demo":"https://firewall-xi.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:59.273Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:59.273Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:59.273Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:43:59.273Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Governance can approve one thing while the implementation that executes does something materially different. Firewall freezes the approved mandate, binds deterministic EVM evidence, applies bounded semantic adjudication, and lets a deterministic policy issue a permit only when the complete semantic contract passes.","Votes, quorum, signatures, timelocks, and calldata validation are necessary, but they do not by themselves prove semantic implementation fidelity. Firewall connects the approved intent to the exact execution package and evidence that will be evaluated."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/GIFTEDLOV/firewall/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"da0cfd26bdd9c90b732c24653e2ca75c65288d1ef21c445de2f6883b7dfe3215","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:59.393Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:59.393Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Governance can approve one thing while the implementation that executes does something materially different. Firewall freezes the approved mandate, binds deterministic EVM evidence, applies bounded semantic adjudication, and lets a deterministic policy issue a permit only when the complete se